WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
Take one cell from an
embryo a few divisions old.

2
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:07.520
It can still become any cell
type, placenta included:

3
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.240
a whole baby.

4
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:13.260
Your bone marrow holds cells
that divide again and again.

5
00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:17.210
Yet no cell from your marrow
could ever build a whole baby.

6
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.750
So why can a cell from an early
embryo build a whole baby,

7
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.830
when a marrow cell can't?

8
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.790
In this mission, you'll find out the
two things that make a cell a stem cell.

9
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.260
Then you'll watch a marrow
cell grow in a dish,

10
00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:32.970
and decide what kind of cell it is.

11
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:37.970
Your mission: explain why a cell from
an early embryo can build a whole baby,

12
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.710
but a marrow cell can't.
